##### Race/ethnicity and U.S. nonresident status
###### Embed this figure
Because students in different racial/ethnic groups earned different shares of overall associate’s degrees conferred, the groups with the highest rates of STEM degrees conferred may not make up the largest shares of all STEM degrees. Of the 84,900 associate’s degrees conferred in a STEM9 field in 2021–22,
*   50 percent were conferred to White students;  
*   21 percent were conferred to Hispanic students;  
*   10 percent each were conferred to Black students and Asian students;  
*   4 percent were conferred to students of Two or more races;  
*   1 percent were conferred to American Indian/Alaska Native students; and  
*   less than one-half of 1 percent were conferred to Pacific Islander students.
Some 3 percent of associate’s degrees in a STEM field were conferred to U.S. nonresident students in 2021–22. [Race/ethnicity ][Nativity/Immigrant/Nonresident]
